<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Perdigao launches Level 1 ADR.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Perdigao launches Level 1 ADR.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Food processor Perdigao S.A. Comercio e Industria said on Thursday it had launched a program of Level One American Depositary Receipts.  </p>
<p>The ADRs will be backed by existing shares and allow the company to be traded in the U.S. over-the-counter market.</p>
<p>Each ADR will represent 5,000 preferred shares. Bank of New York Co Inc will coordinate the operation in the U.S., Perdigao said.</p>
<p>Brazilian bank Itau will be the custodian bank in Brazil, it said.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo Newsroom 55-11-2324411</p>
